| Uniform draw (counter) | — | 1.2 / 0.25 | — |
| Uniform draw (XorShift64 pool) | — | — / 1.31 | — |
| Uniform draw (XorShift1024 pool) | — | — / 2.09 | — |
| Random draw gamma1(2, 0.3), counter | — | 603 / 81 | — |

On CUDA (RTX 4070 SUPER; one MSVC host thread / the GPU, in ns per call):
- Continuous quantiles by root: gaussian1 479 / 139 ns (member 22 / 14 ns); laplace 101 / 22 ns (member 9 / 5 ns); gamma1(\f$2, 0.3\f$) 2964 / 2762 ns (member 460 / 141 ns); gamma1(\f$2, 4\f$) 1941 / 604 ns (member 318 / 102 ns).
- Discrete quantiles by search: poisson(\f$3.5\f$) 2682 / 563 ns.
- Discrete log cdf by summation: poisson(\f$3.5\f$) 780 / 118 ns (member 99 / 33 ns); poisson(\f$40\f$) 2578 / 395 ns (member 160 / 47 ns); poisson(\f$1000\f$) 12761 / 1612 ns (member 91 / 13 ns).
- Expected information in one pass: \f$I\f$ gaussian1 1.5e5 / 1.1e5 ns (hessian), 1.3e5 / 1.1e5 ns (score); \f$\partial^4 I\f$ gaussian1 6.6e6 / 2.7e6 ns (hessian), 4.6e6 / 1.7e6 ns (score); \f$\partial^4 I\f$ gamma1(\f$2, 0.3\f$) 8.0e6 / 6.4e6 ns (hessian), 5.6e6 / 4.3e6 ns (score); \f$\partial^4 I\f$ poisson(\f$3.5\f$) 1.4e4 / 6906 ns (hessian), 1.5e4 / 7578 ns (score). The expected information on CUDA was timed on batches of 256 calls, which leave the GPU almost idle: a single call takes 256 times the figure (28 ms for \f$I\f$ of gaussian1 in the score form).
- Uniform draws: 0.03 ns per call for counter and XorShift64 pool; 0.13 ns per call for XorShift1024 pool.
- Random draws by inversion: gamma1(\f$2, 0.3\f$) 446 / 62 ns.

## Example

The following example generates pseudorandom draws and evaluates the expected Fisher information matrix inside a Kokkos parallel kernel:

\code{.cpp}
#include <laplace/distrib/gamma1.hpp>
#include <laplace/distrib/generic_info.hpp>
#include <laplace/distrib/generic_rng.hpp>
#include <Kokkos_Core.hpp>

void sample_and_info(Kokkos::View<double*>& draws,
                     Kokkos::View<double[3]>& info,
                     int n,
                     std::uint64_t seed) {
  const laplace::distrib::gamma1_distrib d{2.0, 0.3};

  Kokkos::parallel_for("draw_samples", n, KOKKOS_LAMBDA(const int i) {
    draws(i) = laplace::distrib::rng_by_inversion(d, seed, static_cast<std::uint64_t>(i));
  });

  Kokkos::parallel_for("compute_info", 1, KOKKOS_LAMBDA(const int) {
    const auto I = laplace::distrib::distrib_expected_info<0>(d);
    info(0) = I[0];
    info(1) = I[1];
    info(2) = I[2];
  });
}
\endcode

## Module functions

Functions in this module are called as `laplace::distrib::NAME`.

### Expectations and moments
- \ref laplace::distrib::expectation_by_integral "expectation_by_integral()" — expectation \f$\mathbb{E}[h(Y)]\f$ by numerical quadrature or summation
- \ref laplace::distrib::moment_by_integral "moment_by_integral()" — raw or central moment \f$\mathbb{E}[(Y - \mathrm{about})^k]\f$

### Expected information
- \ref laplace::distrib::info_form "info_form" — representation format (hessian or score)
- \ref laplace::distrib::expected_info_result "expected_info_result" — return type for information matrix and derivative tensors
- \ref laplace::distrib::expected_info_by_integral "expected_info_by_integral()" — expected information and derivatives by numerical quadrature or summation
- \ref laplace::distrib::generic_info_form "generic_info_form()" — default representation (`info_form::score`)
- \ref laplace::distrib::distrib_expected_info "distrib_expected_info()" — expected information dispatching to member or generic route

### Discrete cumulative distribution functions
- \ref laplace::distrib::log_cdf_by_sum "log_cdf_by_sum()" — natural logarithm of cumulative distribution function by summation
- \ref laplace::distrib::log_ccdf_by_sum "log_ccdf_by_sum()" — natural logarithm of complementary cumulative distribution function by summation
- \ref laplace::distrib::cdf_by_sum "cdf_by_sum()" — cumulative distribution function by summation
- \ref laplace::distrib::ccdf_by_sum "ccdf_by_sum()" — complementary cumulative distribution function by summation
- \ref laplace::distrib::distrib_cdf "distrib_cdf()" — cumulative distribution function dispatching to member or generic summation
- \ref laplace::distrib::distrib_ccdf "distrib_ccdf()" — complementary cumulative distribution function dispatching to member or generic summation
- \ref laplace::distrib::distrib_log_cdf "distrib_log_cdf()" — natural logarithm of cumulative distribution function dispatching to member or generic summation
- \ref laplace::distrib::distrib_log_ccdf "distrib_log_ccdf()" — natural logarithm of complementary cumulative distribution function dispatching to member or generic summation

### Quantiles
- \ref laplace::distrib::quantile_by_root "quantile_by_root()" — continuous quantile \f$F^{-1}(p)\f$ by root finding
- \ref laplace::distrib::quantile_by_root_from_log "quantile_by_root_from_log()" — continuous quantile from log-probability \f$\log p\f$
- \ref laplace::distrib::quantile_by_root_from_log_upper "quantile_by_root_from_log_upper()" — continuous upper quantile from complementary log-probability \f$\log(1 - p)\f$
- \ref laplace::distrib::quantile_by_search "quantile_by_search()" — discrete quantile by integer search
- \ref laplace::distrib::quantile_by_search_from_log "quantile_by_search_from_log()" — discrete quantile from log-probability \f$\log p\f$
- \ref laplace::distrib::quantile_by_search_from_log_upper "quantile_by_search_from_log_upper()" — discrete upper quantile from complementary log-probability \f$\log(1 - p)\f$
- \ref laplace::distrib::distrib_quantile "distrib_quantile()" — quantile dispatching to member or generic route
- \ref laplace::distrib::distrib_quantile_from_log "distrib_quantile_from_log()" — quantile from \f$\log p\f$ dispatching to member or generic route
- \ref laplace::distrib::distrib_quantile_from_log_upper "distrib_quantile_from_log_upper()" — upper quantile from \f$\log(1 - p)\f$ dispatching to member or generic route

### Random number generation
- \ref laplace::distrib::counter_uniform_source "counter_uniform_source" — SplitMix64 counter-based uniform generator keyed by seed and index
- \ref laplace::distrib::open_unit_uniform "open_unit_uniform()" — open unit interval uniform draw in \f$[2^{-54}, 1 - 2^{-54}]\f$
- \ref laplace::distrib::rng_by_inversion "rng_by_inversion()" — random variate by quantile inversion

